==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schif|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|skif|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skipą}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with Low German {{term|Schipp|lang=nds}}, West Frisian {{term|skip|lang=fy}}, Dutch {{term|schip|lang=nl}}, Yiddish {{term|שיף|tr=shif|lang=yi}}, English {{term|ship|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|skib|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|skepp|lang=sv}}. Related also to Lithuanian {{term|skiẽbti||to rip up|lang=lt}}, Latvian {{term|skibit|škibît|to cut, lop|lang=lv}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

